## Control {{controlId}}: Protect Wireless Access with Authentication and Encryption

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization protects wireless access using authentication and encryption within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Wireless network protection is implemented through WPA2-Enterprise or WPA3 encryption, certificate-based 802.1X authentication, and Intune device configuration profiles that enforce cryptographic protections on all wireless connections accessing CUI resources.

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
Intune device configuration profiles enforce wireless security through {{deviceConfigurationsCount}} configuration policies. Wireless connections are protected with WPA2-Enterprise encryption using AES-256 and authenticated via certificate-based 802.1X protocols. Device configuration profiles distribute trusted root certificates and wireless network profiles that enforce encryption requirements, preventing connections to unprotected or rogue access points.
{{else}}
Intune device configuration profiles for wireless encryption have not been configured. Wireless protection relies on network infrastructure settings pending device-level enforcement.
{{/if}}

